WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.860
James Gunn and Peter Safran's plans for a&nbsp;
brand-new DC film and television universe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:09.120
include self-proclaimed superhero from&nbsp;
the future Booster Gold. With rumors that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:12.660
Chris Pratt could take on the role, fans are&nbsp;
already imagining what that might look like.

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:16.140
The hierarchy of power in the&nbsp;
DC Universe has indeed changed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:20.880
but in a very unexpected way. After taking&nbsp;
12 weeks or so to suss out the direction&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:24.540
of a multibillion-dollar franchise&nbsp;
with nearly a century of backstory,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:29.670
new DC Studios heads Gunn and Safran&nbsp;
have unveiled the start of their shared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:35.350
onscreen universe. And they've confirmed that&nbsp;
Booster Gold is coming. Yes, that Booster Gold.

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:39.720
"He's a fascinating guy. He's a&nbsp;
loser from the future who uses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:42.811
future technology to come back to present day."

00:00:42.811 --> 00:00:47.340
With the announcement of a live-action&nbsp;
small-screen adaptation of the just-shy-of-A-list&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:52.560
hero comes a necessary tsunami of speculation.&nbsp;
At the front of the queue is Chris Pratt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:57.000
who Gunn turned into an international&nbsp;
movie star with 2014's "Guardians of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:01.680
Galaxy." Gunn has already been respectfully&nbsp;
honest about his intention to slap a "dibs"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:05.220
sticker on the backs of performers that&nbsp;
he's previously worked with in the MCU,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:10.080
and that has some fans wondering: Wouldn't it&nbsp;
be crazy if Pratt played a futuristic, immature,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:14.800
wisecracking, perpetually down-on-his-luck&nbsp;
comic book character? You know, again?

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:17.450
"Listen, I'd love to believe&nbsp;
all of this. I really would."

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:21.540
So would a lot of fans! But let's be clear:&nbsp;
There's no announcement that Pratt has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:26.280
cast as of the making of this video. Still, that&nbsp;
hasn't stopped all kinds of online speculation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:31.620
Reddit user clutchkweku has ensured that anyone&nbsp;
eager to see what Chris Pratt might look like as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:36.180
Booster Gold didn't have long to wait with&nbsp;
a post on the Fancast subreddit. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:40.800
the poster seems to have already known something&nbsp;
the rest of us didn't, much like Booster Gold.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:45.120
On December 18, 2022, the fan artist&nbsp;
posted their concept of what Pratt might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:50.520
look like as DC's fifth or sixth favorite time&nbsp;
traveler. Utilizing the AI program Midjourney,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:54.300
this surreal marriage of the famed&nbsp;
raptor wrangler and weirdly shiny,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:58.440
unreal superhero clothes somehow&nbsp;
simultaneously calms and unsettles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:03.000
as if the light on an anglerfish's head was&nbsp;
made out of the star of "The Tomorrow War."

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:07.260
Reactions to the computer-assisted artwork&nbsp;
ran the gamut. One commenter who said,

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:09.744
"I do hate that this works particularly well."

00:02:09.744 --> 00:02:12.000
Another called for a casting swap. saying,

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:13.776
"Chris Pratt should be Aquaman."

00:02:13.776 --> 00:02:18.480
Meanwhile, outside of this particular comments&nbsp;
section, the idea of Pratt making the leap to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:23.880
DC Universe has become quite the debate. Some fans&nbsp;
love the idea, while others, of course, hate it.

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:28.860
Booster Gold first appeared in DC Comics in&nbsp;
1986 in the first issue of his self-titled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:32.700
solo series. The premise was perfect for the&nbsp;
year after "Back to the Future" came out:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:37.320
What if a schlub from the future traveled back&nbsp;
to the past, using the advanced technology of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:42.480
tomorrow to find celebrity and fortune today?&nbsp;
The answer was a fan-favorite mostly-hero with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:47.100
a smarmy streak, who shuffles back and forth&nbsp;
between overconfidence and impostor syndrome.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:50.280
Since his introduction, he's appeared&nbsp;
in two live-action incarnations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:54.060
first played by "Days of Our Lives"&nbsp;
actor Eric Martsolf in an episode of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:57.540
the final season of "Smallville." Donald&nbsp;
Faison later played him in what turned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:00.600
out to be the series finale of the&nbsp;
Arrowverse's "Legends of Tomorrow."

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:04.680
For a better introduction than his live-action&nbsp;
incarnations, check out the "Justice League&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:09.300
Unlimited" episode "The Greatest Story Never&nbsp;
Told," where Booster is voiced by Tom Everett&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:14.252
Scott, and his robot sidekick Skeets is portrayed&nbsp;
by Billy West, who was Fry on "Futurama."

00:03:14.252 --> 00:03:18.032
"'They also serve who only&nbsp;
stand and wait.' John Milton."

00:03:18.032 --> 00:03:22.800
"Oh yeah? I got one for you.&nbsp;
'This stinks.' Booster Gold."

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:26.880
While Chris Pratt playing Booster Gold&nbsp;
is still fan speculation at this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:31.385
it's clear that if he is cast, Bradley&nbsp;
Cooper will have to voice Skeets, right?

